
### 1. Z-Ordering — Simple Explanation

**Interview answer:**

> “Z-Ordering is a data layout optimization technique in Databricks. It colocates related data based on one or more columns, so when I query using those columns, Databricks can skip unnecessary files and scan less data.”

### Simple example

Suppose we have a customer table:

| customer_id | country | amount |
|---|---|---:|
| 101 | India | 500 |
| 102 | USA | 700 |
| 103 | India | 300 |
| ... | ... | ... |

If most of our queries are:

```sql
SELECT *
FROM customer
WHERE customer_id = 101;
```

We can use:

```sql
OPTIMIZE customer
ZORDER BY (customer_id);
```

Databricks reorganizes the files so that records with similar `customer_id` values are placed closer together.

So instead of reading **many files**, Databricks can **skip irrelevant files**.

### Think of it like this

Without Z-Ordering:

> 📚 Books are randomly distributed across 100 shelves.

With Z-Ordering:

> 📚 Books with similar topics are organized closer together.

If I need a particular topic, I don't need to search all 100 shelves.

